    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1240-a1">

                <pb facs="0996" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg880"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief Inspector to Vice Consul Bevan</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to your note of the 5th instant,
                    I inform you that the provisional permit that I granted to the Cortez Oil
                    Corporation does not imply that the said corporation must submit beforehand to
                    laws and regulations of which it has no knowledge; it only stipulates that the
                    permit is of a provisional character good only until the new oil laws go into
                    effect, whereupon the said corporation will have to request a new permit,
                    submitting to the law which will then have been brought to its notice.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Cabrera.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
